---
description: Asset import conventions for sprites, textures, and FBX models
globs: ["**/*.png", "**/*.fbx", "**/*.jpg"]
alwaysApply: false
---

- Don't assume Unity's automatic Sprite slicing ("Full Rect"/auto) is correct. Do: use
  manual Sprite Slicing and have me review the slice rects.
- Don't mark an FBX import "done" without checking: object origin = geometry origin,
  transforms applied, smoothing matches intent, poly count within mobile budget, textures
  match the render pipeline.
- If normals look broken, shading is inverted, or edges look hard: check import normal
  calculation and smoothness settings before suggesting a re-export from Blender/Maya.
- Don't leave texture compression on generic "Automatic." Do: set per-platform overrides
  (Android/iOS) and turn mipmaps off for 2D sprites/UI.
